{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790509298,"nonce":"f8AktlKG8r7exmDmNtgzo5JjvBM=","title":"wasm AOT: a program LLVM lowers to a libm call the runtime object lacks fails to link","message":"`wlift --aot k.wasm --aot-target wasm32-wasip1 bench/k_nucleotide.wren`:\n\n    link failed: the program needs env.exp2, which the runtime object does\n    not define, so it does not match this wlift. ...\n\nk_nucleotide computes `4.pow(k - 1)`; LLVM rewrites pow of a constant base\ninto exp2, a libm call. The runtime object is prelinked with `-lc`, which\npulls in only the libc members the runtime itself references, so exp2 is\nabsent. Any libm function LLVM introduces (exp2, exp10, sincos, ldexp,\n...) can hit this.\n\nFix: force-include the libm entry points LLVM may emit when prelinking\nthe runtime object (`-u exp2 -u ...` in .github/actions/wasm-runtime and\nthe README's steps), as Ash does with LIBRARY_LIBC; the linker's tree\nshaking drops the ones a program never calls. Also make link_error say\n\"not in the runtime object\" without claiming a version mismatch when the\nmissing name is a libc/libm function.","files":null}]}